; TRIPWIRE FIXTURE. Generating from this MUST fail, on the consumer backend,
; with a message naming the reason.
;
; It goes green — i.e. the generator starts accepting it — only when someone
; teaches the host path to tell an empty optional apart from a failed call.
; Read lidlCheckOptionalReturns before deleting this file: the fix is to NARROW
; the null-means-failure rule to methods whose published metadata declares an
; optional return, never to delete that rule (deleting it silently converts
; every pre-existing failure into a success).
module refusing_module {
  version "1.0.0"
  method lookup(id: tstr) -> ?tstr
}
